{"run": "0090", "session": "0014-horizon-ajcr-p4", "inbox": {"items": [{"id": "I-1469", "title": "LIVE MID-SESSION AT ajcr-p4: the shared index would revert MY OWN LAST COMMIT, and the entry is a staged M against a stale blob -- no D line, so a lane grepping ^D sees a clean index. Nothing lost yet.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 1, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-30T03:05:05.808260+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1465", "title": "FOUR ROWS AND FIVE FILES PRICE THE SEAM'S TWO ANTECEDENTS AS TWO CONDITIONS TO BE MET AT SOME LUCKY V. THEY ARE ONE CONDITION: at a one-chart atlas the pair says exactly that the chart map is an ISO of big-Zariski sheaves, by one mathlib instance nobody had used here.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 1, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-30T03:03:36.204562+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1476", "title": "LIVE AT ajc-p2 SESSION END: the shared index would REVERT my own audit-correction commit and 176 lines of an AJCR proof file. Nothing lost yet. Enumerated with the command per I-1222, not quoted from any lane's count.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 1, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-30T03:02:03.927900+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1467", "title": "THE 01JJ GLUING ENGINE IS BYPASSED AT A ONE-CHART ATLAS -- may reprice what dat-glue and the JacobianData fields owe.", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-30T02:43:47.885393+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1466", "title": "THE 01JJ GLUING ENGINE IS BYPASSED AT A ONE-CHART ATLAS -- may reprice what dat-glue and the JacobianData fields owe.", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-30T02:43:43.178318+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1452", "title": "COVERAGE AT THE LEDGER PARAMETER NOW COSTS ONE ARITHMETIC FACT ABOUT THE GENUS -- relevant to cover-noninj and to any V-interval reasoning, and it changes what 'coverage is available' means.", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 1, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-30T02:06:24.492856+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1453", "title": "CLAIM ajcr-p4 (run 0090 r6): AJCR.w4-rep.datum.chart-restrict -- the INHABITATION question that four rows now name as the one thing gating the whole antecedent-1 side, and which no lane has ever attacked directly.", "kind": "info", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-30T02:05:44.807982+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1429", "title": "A \"TWO DIFFERENT OBJECTS, UNRELATED IN THE TREE\" RESIDUE IS THE ONE TO TEST FIRST WHEN THE TWO OBJECTS ARE A BASE CHANGE APART -- base change along the IDENTITY extension k -> k is an isomorphism, and the transport is usually already landed under a name that mentions neither object.", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-30T01:36:03.065216+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1276", "title": "THE univSeed STRADDLING PROBE U2 SAYS \"NOBODY HAS RUN IN TWO ROUNDS\" IS THE WRONG QUESTION -- the seed's cover is chart-subordinate BY CONSTRUCTION, as a structure FIELD, so measuring its support decides nothing.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-30T01:12:52.295411+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1329", "title": "THE COVERAGE THRESHOLD IS UNIFORM IN THE SPLITTING FIELD AND PI-FREE -- two files price B-5 step 3's residue against a per-fibre threshold they treat as unobtainable, and the tree has had the pi-free form all along.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-30T01:00:43.331697+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1349", "title": "REFUTED: \"no relCurve C L to P1 L exists in this tree\" -- it is three haveI away, and DAT-0a IS instantiable at L. I-1329 and two docstrings now assert the false half as the measured one.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-30T01:00:38.400281+00:00"}], "created": 5, "comments": 4, "actions": 5, "total": 11}, "roadmap": {"items": [{"id": "AJCR.w4-rep", "title": "Wave 4: representability of Pic^0 (curve-specialised Kleiman)", "status": "active", "created": false, "status_changes": 0, "status_to": "", "comments": 2, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-30T03:03:33.443261+00:00"}, {"id": "AJCR.w4-rep.datum.chart-restrict", "title": "CHART-RESTRICT: the restricted-chart fibre criterion + the V-coupling to coverage (repairs the only route to antecedent 1)", "status": "pending", "created": false, "status_changes": 1, "status_to": "active", "comments": 3, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-30T03:03:19.388565+00:00"}], "created": 0, "status_changes": 1, "comments": 5, "total": 2}, "commits": [{"sha": "6b952a5e4826b7d4cddccfe6963c8c3dbc8c7a1a", "short_sha": "6b952a5e48", "subject": "AJCR: give the REASON the seam collapse stops at one chart, not just the assertion", "summary": "", "created_at": "2026-07-30T11:07:21+08:00", "role": "horizon", "kind": "agent", "files": [{"path": "MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild/AlgebraicJacobian/Picard/Pic0ChartSeamCollapse.lean", "category": "lean", "add": 10, "del": 2, "loc_before": 515, "loc_after": 523, "loc_code_before": 173, "loc_code_after": 173, "sorry_before": 0, "sorry_after": 0, "sorry_delta": 0, "decl_before": {"theorem": 12, "def": 3}, "decl_after": {"theorem": 12, "def": 3}, "decl_delta": {}, "added": false, "deleted": false}], "lean": {"files": 1, "add": 10, "del": 2, "loc_after": 523, "loc_code_after": 173, "loc_delta": 8, "loc_code_delta": 0, "sorry_after": 0, "sorry_delta": 0, "decl_after": {"theorem": 12, "def": 3}, "decl_delta": {}}, "blueprint": {"files": 0, "add": 0, "del": 0, "loc_after": 0, "loc_code_after": 0, "loc_delta": 0, "loc_code_delta": 0, "sor